  "methods": [
    "Unchanged executables and runtime settings across requested eco modes; seven timed GEMMs after two warmups",
    "One node per job, fixed 48 compute threads split over 1, 2, or 4 MPI ranks",
    "Aggregate throughput uses the slowest rank duration; identical per-rank shapes, not fixed-work strong scaling",
    "Native Fortran/SSL2 and LLVM C++/interoperable Fujitsu BLAS run sequentially on the same node within each job"
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Eco comparisons are separate jobs on different nodes, not a repeated same-node paired experiment",
    "Clock frequencies and eco modes are scheduler requests; hardware clock and throttling were not independently measured",
    "The earlier native and LLVM drivers use different inputs, initialization, and BLAS interfaces",
    "4-rank LLVM 8192-cube cases show severe slowdowns; the two eco-on controls lack complete LLVM results and OVERALL=PASS, despite wrapper exit-code files containing zero",
    "All three eco-off LLVM runs include all ten numerical cases and OVERALL=PASS; all native SSL2 runs recorded all four cases and allowed the script to proceed to LLVM",
    "Process CPU-time core-count diagnostics are unreliable and excluded"
